        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Lost Heir',
            subtitle: 'The Victorian City Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Lost Heir is a historical bidding and trick-taking game that gained massive popularity in the late 19th century in North America. Produced by McLoughlin Brothers (and later Milton Bradley), it features a custom deck where suits are named after major cities (e.g., New York, Boston, Chicago, Philadelphia). The game centers around two pivotal cards: the 'Lost Heir' (bonus points) and the 'Wrong Boy' (penalty points). It combines the bidding strategy of Pinochle with the capture mechanics of Authors.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Based on the 1872 novel 'The Lost Heir of Linlithgow'. McLoughlin Bros. patented the game in 1893.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '4 players in two partnerships (Standard).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '48 cards (typically). Suits: New York, Philadelphia, Chicago, Boston. Ranks: Mayor (High), Judge, Policeman, etc.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Custom deck and score sheet.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards are dealt out; a bidding phase follows.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'Canadian Lost Heir: Features Toronto, Halifax, Winnipeg, Montreal.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: "L'HÃ©ritier Perdu: French-Canadian variant with identical rules.",
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'City Bidding: A modern abstract variant.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
